{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 35, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e2b-it", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was a powerful figure in the Crusader states during the 12th century. He ruled the County of Tripoli from 1144 to 1193 effectively becoming the ruler of a substantial territory in the Levant. His reign marked a period of significant expansion and consolidation of Tripoli's power and influence. Raymond III was a key player in the Crusades and his actions had lasting consequences for the region.\n\n*Early Life and Ascension* Raymond III was born in 1106 the son of Raymond II Count of Tripoli. He inherited the county following his father's death in 1144. His early reign was characterized by consolidating his power and dealing with internal rivalries. He strengthened the county's defenses and fostered economic growth. He was known for his military prowess and diplomatic skills establishing Tripoli as a respected power among its neighbors. Raymond III also actively participated in the Crusades contributing troops and resources to various campaigns.\n\nHis reign saw Tripoli expand its territory significantly. He gained control of several coastal cities and fortified positions transforming Tripoli into a major trading hub. The county’s control extended over parts of Syria and Palestine offering a strategic advantage in the ongoing conflict between the Crusaders and the Muslim powers. Raymond III fostered trade relations with various European powers and established a thriving economy based on agriculture and maritime commerce. He was a patron of the arts and sciences supporting scholars and artists in Tripoli.\n\n*Military Campaigns and Conflicts* Raymond III’s reign was marked by numerous military campaigns and conflicts. He actively defended Tripoli against various attacks from Muslim forces including the Zengi and Saladin dynasties. He led expeditions to support the Crusader states in the Holy Land and participated in several sieges and battles. He engaged in conflicts with the Seljuk Turks and other Muslim powers securing Tripoli's borders and maintaining its independence. His military campaigns were often costly but ultimately successful in preserving Tripoli's autonomy. He employed a combination of military strategy and diplomacy to achieve his objectives.\n\nRaymond III's legacy is complex. He is remembered as a strong and effective ruler who defended Tripoli's independence and fostered its economic prosperity. However his reign also involved significant military expenditure and conflict. His policies sometimes strained relations with neighboring powers. Despite these challenges Raymond III left a lasting mark on the County of Tripoli solidifying its position as a significant power in the Levant for many years. He died in 1193 leaving behind a stable and prosperous county. His reign represents a crucial period in the history of the Crusader states and the Levant.\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "Raymond", "logprob": -0.1804991215467453}, {"token": "▁III", "logprob": -1.6689286894688848e-06}, {"token": "▁Count", "logprob": -6.115249561844394e-05}, {"token": "▁of", "logprob": -2.861018856492592e-06}, {"token": "▁Tripoli", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "▁was", "logprob": -0.08474750816822052}, {"token": "▁a", "logprob": -0.03216259181499481}, {"token": "▁powerful", "logprob": -0.5099871158599854}, {"token": "▁figure", "logprob": -1.482170820236206}, {"token": "▁in", "logprob": -0.01998409442603588}, {"token": "▁the", "logprob": -0.0038492411840707064}, {"token": "▁Crus", "logprob": -1.5466989278793335}, {"token": "ader", "logprob": -0.3132883310317993}, {"token": "▁states", "logprob": -0.06137482449412346}, {"token": "▁during", "logprob": -0.4115596413612366}, {"token": "▁the", "logprob": -4.7444173105759546e-05}, {"token": "▁", "logprob": -0.007950328290462494}, {"token": "1", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": "2", "logprob": -0.0031881716568022966}, {"token": "th", "logprob": 0.